# Terraform quality & naming

Format with `terraform fmt` (`task format:terraform`). Validate with `task infra:validate`.

## Layout

```
infra/
  envs/<environment>/   # roots (develop, …) — backend, providers, module wiring
  modules/<name>/       # reusable modules (api, db, ui)
```

- Split module files by concern: `ec2.tf`, `acm.tf`, `s3.tf`, `iam.tf`, `variables.tf`, `outputs.tf`, `versions.tf`.
- Env roots wire modules; put reusable logic in `modules/`, not copy-paste across envs.

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Examples |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Resources, data, modules, variables, locals, outputs | `snake_case` | `api_parameter_prefix`, `cloudfront_price_class` |
| Module directories | short `snake` / single token | `api`, `db`, `ui` |
| Env directories | environment name | `develop`, `production` |
| AWS name tags / Name values | include `project` + `environment` (+ component) | via variables `project`, `environment` |

- Variables: always set `description` and `type`; defaults only when safe.
- Locals: computed names and shared prefixes (`local.api_parameter_prefix`), not raw duplication.
- Outputs: stable, useful names for Task/scripts (`api_url`, `api_ecr_repository_url`).

## Quality

- Prefer **modules + variables** over hard-coded account-specific values in modules.
- Don’t put secrets in Terraform state when avoidable (Clerk secret → SSM via `task api:secrets:push`).
- Security groups / IAM: least privilege; comment non-obvious couplings (see develop `main.tf` parameter-prefix note).
- After structural changes, run `task infra:validate ENV=…` (and plan before apply).
- Keep provider aliases explicit (`aws.us_east_1` for ACM/CloudFront certs).
